<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the bundle's own Info.plist by Tauri's bundler.

  These keys are not optional: macOS kills a process that reaches for the
  microphone, Bluetooth or camera without one, rather than refusing the
  request, so a missing key presents as the app disappearing. The sentence is
  what the system prompt shows, so it says what the access is for.

  Everything past the microphone is for web pages in the in-app browser.
  Bluetooth is a passkey's "Use phone or tablet" (hybrid transport). Camera
  and location are refused anyway until Entitlements.plist grants them under
  the hardened runtime; the strings are here so a page asking can never crash.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
  <dict>
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Dray transcribes what you say into the composer. Audio is processed on this Mac and never leaves it.</string>
    <key>NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Websites in Dray's browser use Bluetooth to sign in with a passkey on your phone or tablet.</string>
    <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Websites in Dray's browser may ask to use your camera.</string>
    <key>NSLocationUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Websites in Dray's browser may ask for your location.</string>
    <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Websites in Dray's browser may ask for your location.</string>
  </dict>
</plist>
